          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भोज्यम् — bhojyam — \"eatables; food\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि अतिथयः आगच्छन्ति, तर्हि बहु भोज्यं पचामः। yadi atithayaḥ āgacchanti, tarhi bahu bhojyaṃ pacāmaḥ. If the guests come, we will cook a lot of food."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भोज्यम् (bhojyam) comes from the root √bhuj, \"to enjoy, to eat\", with the ending -ya; MW gives bhojya as eatable, what is eaten (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
